# Offer, QR, settlement

Services and packages have **price** and **duration**. Duration drives the queue; price drives the offer.

## Split (canonical example)

Walk-in package **250**. Salon funds **20%** for the app → gap **50**, split 50/50.

- Walk-in pays **250**, platform fee **0**
- App-acquired **after customer QR scan** pays **225**, platform fee **25** (ledger, not taken from the drawer)

## Visit paths

| Path | Check-in | Customer QR scan | Pays | Platform fee |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| App-acquired | Already in queue/system | Required | 225 | 25 |
| Walk-in | Cashier enters them | None | 250 | 0 |

No scan ⇒ no discount. The customer demands the scan to get the saving. Reception has no reason to hide walk-ins: recording them costs nothing and keeps the **queue complete**.

## Money

Customer pays **cash to the salon**. Accumulate platform fees. One **monthly settlement** (wallet, InstaPay, or transfer).

QR is **rotating**, on the reception screen, scanned by the **customer device**. That scan is independent visit proof for settlement.

## Ranking

Public salon rating orders the app list. **QR scan count** lifts rank so the salon pushes the app itself.
